    "done_when": "Cache the picker's budget view on the stamps of the files it reads, so a dispatch stops paying 0.2-0.6 s to rebuild it. The snapshot-stall investigation (~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/snapshot-stall-under-load/report.md and timings.json) measured reckon/crew/picker/snapshot.py budget_view (line 391) at 286 ms median idle and 343 ms under load, at most 614 ms. Of that, budget.preflight takes 203-243 ms and budget.recorded_windows 81-97 ms.\n\n1. First confirm the cost still reproduces on main, by timing budget_view five times against project reckon's live state, and record the figures.\n2. Cache budget_view's file-derived result through the stamped pick-input cache that routing.context_census and routing._estimated_hours already use, keyed on the stamps of every file it reads: the paid-lanes document, the budget-resets record, lane documents and the ledger files it reads. Recompute every time-derived field on each call, including ages, stale flags, days to reset and anything computed from now, so a cached entry never serves a stale age.\n3. Tests in tests/test_budget_view_is_cached.py:\n   - Equality: the cached and uncached results are identical for a fixture.\n   - Second call: an unchanged second call reads none of the input files, counted with an instrumented open or stat.\n   - Stamp: touching the paid-lanes document changes the result.\n   - Age: advancing a frozen clock changes the age fields, but not the cached file-derived ones.\n4. Record budget_view's median and maximum before and after, five calls each, in the manifest.\n5. Negative control: dropping the per-call recompute of the age fields makes the age test fail.\n\nDo not edit reckon/crew/dispatch.py or reckon/cli.py; they are on hold for a module split. Gate: tests/test_budget_view_is_cached.py, every tests/test_picker*.py, tests/test_pick_candidates_one_pass.py, tests/test_estimated_hours_reads_one_plan.py, and every tests/ file that imports reckon.budget or reckon.crew.budget_group. Build that list from your head tree with grep -l. Run with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 6 in the FOREGROUND, with one log each for base and head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta. Write the evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/one-typesafe-model-picker/budget-view-is-cached.html.",
    "estimated_hours": 1.5,
    "goal": "The picker's budget view is cached on its input files' stamps, with ages recomputed per call",
